      <description align="center" color="transparent" colored="true" height="122" resized="false" width="180" x="881" y="349">In the PI Pulling Block, data is fetched from the PI server&lt;br&gt;O/P: PI data</description>
      <description align="center" color="red" colored="true" height="592" resized="true" width="420" x="11" y="10">Feature get PI data&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Author:&lt;br&gt;Akshay Hasabe&lt;br&gt;Naveen Kumar&lt;br&gt;Karthik Sangappalli&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Overview:&lt;br&gt;The PI pulling block retrieves timestamped data from PI servers using macros and input parameters that define the time window and tag details. It connects to specified servers and fetches data for the given PI tags, preparing it for downstream processing.&lt;br/&gt;Inputs:&lt;br/&gt;1. pi tags&lt;br/&gt;2. Pipeline parameters&lt;br/&gt;Input macros:&lt;br/&gt;1. end_time&lt;br/&gt;2. connection_pi&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;Output:&lt;br/&gt;1. Pi_data&lt;br&gt;</description>
    </process>
  </operator>
